# Existing entries
# BOTH forms are required. `node_modules/` (trailing slash) matches a
# DIRECTORY only — it does NOT match a symlink named `node_modules`, which is
# what you get when a worktree links to a sibling checkout's install to skip
# `npm ci`. That gap let a machine-specific absolute-path symlink
# (`node_modules -> /Users/<someone>/emdash/repositories/ace/node_modules`)
# get committed to main in PR #956. On the next worktree it resolved into a
# `node_modules/node_modules` loop, and every vitest run in that tree died
# with exit 194 and ZERO output — no error, no stack, nothing to grep. Cost
# most of a live device session to find. Keep both lines.
node_modules/
node_modules
.gws-sa-key.json

# Environment secrets — only .env.tpl (1Password-injectable) is committed;
# real .env files with actual team ids, tokens, and experiment ids must
# never land in git.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Temporary scripts and artifacts from live-OCS verification sessions.
# These contain exploration code and HTML dumps that shouldn't live in git.
scripts/tmp/

# Claude Code session-local settings (per-developer, not shared state)
.claude/settings.local.json
.gstack/

# Per-run test-audit artifacts from /canopy:test-audit. These are large
# (corpus.yaml is megabytes) and re-generatable; the audit-report.md /
# architecture-review.md content lives in the PR body.
.canopy/test-audits/
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Phase 7 synthetic walkthrough artifacts. These are per-run rendered
# decks (HTML + JSON, 1-2MB each) and per-run spec YAMLs. Authoritative
# copies live in Drive under ACE/<opp>/runs/<run-id>/7-synthetic/; the
# local filesystem copy is a side-effect of the walkthrough renderer.
docs/walkthroughs/
screenshots/
# The phase folder itself lands at the repo root, not under docs/ — a run
# leaves `7-synthetic/realized.json` (the realized par_url map) behind. It
# was NOT matched by the two rules above, so every run since has dirtied
# `git status` and had to be hand-excluded from each PR. Same authoritative
# copy in Drive; same reasoning.
7-synthetic/

# canopy DDD per-run bootstrap context. Names one run and its Drive folder
# id, so it is regenerated every run and never durable. Its SIBLING
# `.canopy/ddd/learnings.md` is deliberately NOT ignored: it accumulates
# cross-run findings and is tracked, exactly like `.canopy/pm/learnings.md`.
# Ignoring the whole `ddd/` directory would silently bury them.
.canopy/ddd/context.md

# Phase 6 per-opp test recipes (generated by app-test-cases per run; not source palettes)
mcp/mobile/recipes/static/J[0-9]*.yaml
mcp/mobile/recipes/static/J[0-9]*[a-z].yaml

# ephemeral Claude Code worktrees
.claude/worktrees/

# Python bytecode (a stray .pyc was committed once; the checker tests import
# scripts/check-summary-links.py, which regenerates it)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# /ace:connect-opp-create working files. The spec names a live Connect program
# and HQ apps; the run record carries FLW PHONE NUMBERS in cleartext (the API
# key is elided, the numbers cannot be — they are the payload). Both land in
# whatever directory the operator ran from, which is often a checkout, so
# `git add .` would pick them up.
*-connect-opp-spec.yaml
*-opp-spec.yaml
*-created.yaml
dry-run-connect-opp-create.md
